// M7e Cold War scenario (1987): a Blue tank and TOW-IFV team holds a village in wooded uplands
// against a Red tank-heavy combined-arms attack from the north-east. M1s (105 mm) face T-72As
// (125 mm): neither side can count on its armour, and forest breaks up the long sight lines the
// M1's thermal sight would otherwise exploit. Play as Blue: occupy battle positions (B), set
// weapons control, use the planning phase. The Blue AI plan is used only when the side is not
// player-controlled (headless runs, tests).
(
    id: "cw-village-defence",
    name: "VILLAGE DEFENCE",
    date: (1987, 6, 15),
    start_time_s: 21600, // 06:00
    map: (id: "uplands", recipe: "wooded-uplands", seed: 7, size_m: 8000.0),
    seed: 5,
    briefing: "SITUATION: A RED TANK-HEAVY FORCE (T-72 TANKS AND INFANTRY FIGHTING VEHICLES) ADVANCES FROM THE NORTH-EAST THROUGH THE FORESTED HILLS AT FIRST LIGHT.\n\nMISSION: 1ST AND 2ND PLATOONS (M1) AND 3RD PLATOON (M2 BRADLEY, TOW) HOLD THE VILLAGE FOR 45 MINUTES. RED WINS BY HOLDING THE VILLAGE UNCONTESTED FOR 2 MINUTES. A SIDE THAT LOSES 70 % OF ITS VEHICLES LOSES.\n\nNOTES: THE M1 AND THE T-72A CAN DEFEAT EACH OTHER FRONTALLY AT 2 KM, BUT THE FOREST LIMITS SIGHT LINES TO A FEW HUNDRED METRES IN PLACES. USE HULL-DOWN POSITIONS ON THE EDGE OF THE TREES, DISTRIBUTE FIRES, AND KEEP THE TOW VEHICLES BEHIND THE TANKS UNTIL RED DEPLOYS.",
    objectives: [(name: "VILLAGE", centre: (3840.0, 3370.0), radius_m: 300.0)],
